  ],
  "comments": [
    {
      "paragraph_index": 2,
      "comment": "The final medium is prepared from 320 ml basal broth by the addition of 40 ml horse serum and 40 ml swine serum (20% total serum)."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 3,
      "comment": "For primary isolation, 25% serum is beneficial for M. hyopneumoniae and M. flocculare, and 15% for M. hyorhinis, with the pH adjusted to 7.3."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 4,
      "comment": "For improved antibacterial effects, add 0.15 mg/ml of cycloserine and, if necessary, a further 0.2 mg/ml of vancomycin and 0.005 mg/ml of nalidixic acid."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 5,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 7,
      "comment": "Dispense in volumes of 320 ml as basal broth and store at -2 5 °C (will keep for at least one year)."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 8,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 10,
      "comment": "Dispense among 7 one-litre infusion bottles and autoclave at 120°C for one min, or at 110°C for 20 min. Pool again."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 11,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 13,
      "comment": "For use: 25 ml stock A, 400 ml of water, 25 ml stock B, add more water to 500 ml."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 14,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 16,
      "comment": "Dissolve in 400 ml water, add 1.4 g of CaCl 2 (anhydrous) and water up to 500 ml."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 17,
      "comment": "This stock solutions are heated to 90°C and kept for 5-10 min."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 18,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 20,
      "comment": "Dissolve in 400 ml water, add 0.6 g of KH2PO4 and water up to 500 ml."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 21,
      "comment": "This stock solutions are heated to 90°C and kept for 5-10 min."
    }
  ]
}